Implement the following save-system, start-screen, and intro-flow changes.

The goal is to simplify persistence so that gameplay progress is ONLY persisted when the player explicitly saves, while Intro Part A and Intro Part B become one complete intro sequence.

Do not redesign unrelated gameplay systems.

==================================================
1. CORE SAVE-SYSTEM RULE
==================================================

Change the gameplay save system from automatic saving to explicit manual saving.

The LAST MANUALLY SAVED SaveState must be the single persistent source of truth for gameplay progress.

During normal gameplay, React/runtime state may change freely, but these changes must NOT automatically be written to browser storage.

If the player reloads the page, closes the browser, Vite performs a reload, or the game is reopened:

→ discard unsaved runtime progress
→ load the last manually saved SaveState

If no manually saved SaveState exists:

→ start as a fresh game


