==================================================

Do NOT set introPartBDone = true after Intro Part A.

Only set:

introPartBDone = true

when Intro Part B has fully completed.

This changes the CURRENT RUNTIME STATE only.

Do NOT immediately call writeSave() when Intro B finishes.

The completed intro becomes persistent only when the player later explicitly uses:

Settings → Save Game


Example:

Fresh game
→ Intro A
→ Intro B
→ Intro B completes
→ runtime introPartBDone = true
→ player plays normally
→ Settings → Save Game
→ saved SaveState now contains introPartBDone: true


Next launch:

Continue
→ saved introPartBDone === true
→ skip Intro A
→ skip Intro B
→ normal gameplay


==================================================
12. RELOADING BEFORE SAVING
==================================================

This behavior is intentional:

Fresh game
→ Intro A
→ Intro B
→ Intro completes
→ player does NOT manually save
→ reload

Because no manual save exists:

→ start fresh again
→ Intro A runs again
→ Intro B runs again


Similarly:

Load an older manual save with introPartBDone === false
→ play intro
→ do not save
→ reload

The previous manual save still has:

introPartBDone === false

Therefore:

→ complete intro runs again


Do NOT add automatic intro persistence to prevent this.

This is intentional manual-save behavior.


